---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { DAY_PLAN, CARD_PLAN } from "../content/schema.mjs";
---

<Base title="About this site" description="How the PACU rotation curriculum is built and what its labels mean.">
  <main>
    <header class="masthead">
      <p class="kicker">About</p>
      <h1>How this site is built</h1>
    </header>
    <div class="body">
      <p>
        This is a {DAY_PLAN.length}-day reading curriculum for the post-anesthesia care unit (PACU) rotation, written for
        anesthesiology residents and the trainees who rotate with them. Each day states one claim, names the kind of evidence
        it rests on, and cites every number to an entry in a source ledger. The ledger entry carries the citation, the design
        of the study, and a link to the DOI, the PubMed record, or the regulatory or society document it came from.
      </p>
      <h2>What the labels mean</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Trial based</strong> means randomized evidence supports the claim as stated. <strong>Consensus only</strong>
        means it does not, and the chip says what the claim rests on instead: physiology, registry data, a guideline, a
        practice advisory, or expert consensus. That is the common case in perioperative medicine and it is not a failure
        state. Two further chips say whether the mechanism is settled and whether the clinical claim has survived testing.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>DRAFT</strong> means the rotation director has not yet cleared the page. Nothing on a draft page should be
        used clinically. <strong>Local practice differs</strong> marks a point where institutions do things differently; the
        page says so rather than asserting one answer.
      </p>
      <h2>What is not here</h2>
      <p>
        No figures reproduced from any source. No hosted PDFs. No accounts and no saved progress; the quizzes are formative
        and answers vanish when you leave the page. The {CARD_PLAN.length} algorithm cards restate material from their parent day; they are a bedside layout of it, not new evidence.
      </p>
      <h2>Privacy</h2>
      <p>
        The site is static. Cloudflare, which hosts it, collects anonymous, cookie-less page-view counts. Nothing else is
        collected, and nothing you do on a quiz leaves your browser.
      </p>
      <p class="note">Educational material only. Not clinical decision support and not a substitute for institutional protocol.</p>
    </div>
  </main>
</Base>
